    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d230">

                <pb facs="0666" n="452" sameAs="frus:frus1871/pg452"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 213.</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Schenck to Mr.
                        Fish</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 43.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1871-08-08"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 8, 1871</date>. (Received August
                    21.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> You will have noted the discussion which
                    took place in the House of Commons on Friday last, the 4th instant, on the
                    motion of Sir Charles Adderley for the production of copies of instructions
                    given by Her Majesty’s government to their commissioners at Washington. I now
                    send you, in form for preservation, a full report of that debate, taken from the
                    London Times of last Saturday.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ROB’T C. SCHENCK.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d230-a1.xml" xpointer="d230-a1"/>
            </div>
